# Documentation

Applies to projects that keep a `docs/` folder — skip it when the project has none.

These projects are **AI-driven**. Persistent docs in `docs/` carry context across sessions. Agent rules in `agents/rules/` define coding style; docs define product and architecture knowledge.

## Docs vs rules

| Location | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `docs/` | What to build — architecture, features, ADRs, workflows |
| `agents/rules/` | How to write code — TypeScript, React, imports, tests |
| `AGENTS.md` | Agent entry point — conventions, commands, doc index |

## Before implementing

1. Read [docs/README.md](../../docs/README.md)
2. Read [docs/spec/saas-template-spec.md](../../docs/spec/saas-template-spec.md) for product requirements
3. Read [docs/architecture/feature-driven-development.md](../../docs/architecture/feature-driven-development.md) for where code lives inside features
4. Read [docs/architecture/security.md](../../docs/architecture/security.md) before handling user input or AI integrations
5. Read the relevant [docs/features/](../../docs/features/) doc when working in a feature
6. Read related [ADRs](../../docs/adr/) before changing an architectural decision

## When to update docs

- **New feature** — create `docs/features/<feature>.md` from the template in [docs/features/README.md](../../docs/features/README.md)
- **Route or public API change** — update the feature doc
- **Architecture or major library choice** — update architecture overview and add an ADR
- **New env var or external integration** — document in the feature doc or an ADR
- **Completed or started plan task** — update [docs/status/current-task.md](../../docs/status/current-task.md) and plan checkboxes
- **User-facing behavior verified** — update [docs/status/application.md](../../docs/status/application.md)

Skip doc updates for trivial refactors that do not change behavior agents need to know.

## After implementing (checklist)

Before considering work done, confirm docs are current:

- [ ] Read the relevant feature doc **before** coding
- [ ] Updated `docs/features/<feature>.md` if routes, public API, flows, or integrations changed
- [ ] Updated `docs/status/current-task.md` and plan checkboxes if task progress changed
- [ ] Updated `docs/status/application.md` if user-visible behavior changed
- [ ] Added or updated an ADR for architectural decisions
- [ ] Staged doc updates in the **same commit** as code (pre-commit runs the `check:docs-drift` script)

Run `/rcrdk-review-rules` before merge to catch docs drift on the full branch.

## Docs drift (pre-commit)

The `check:docs-drift` script runs on pre-commit (see `package.json` for the exact command). It fails when:

- Production files (`src/features/<feature>/`, or the project's domain folders) are staged without any `docs/` update in the same commit
- App routes (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `route.ts`) change without a staged doc touch
- `src/env.ts` changes without a staged doc touch

Allowed doc paths that satisfy the check: `docs/features/`, `docs/status/`, `docs/architecture/`, `docs/spec/`, `docs/superpowers/`, `docs/runbooks/`, `docs/workflows/`, `docs/adr/`.

## Feature doc location

Mirror feature folder names:

```
src/features/auth/     →  docs/features/auth.md
src/features/billing/  →  docs/features/billing.md
```

## ADRs

Use [docs/adr/README.md](../../docs/adr/README.md) format. Filename: `NNNN-short-title.md`. Add a row to the ADR index.

## Writing style

- Short, factual, and scannable
- Prefer tables and lists over long prose
- Link to code paths (`src/features/...`) and related docs
- Keep docs in sync with code — outdated docs are worse than none
